Roman Dolidze vs. Anthony Hernandez: Bloody Elbow predictions suggest that 'Fluffy' will be too much for the Georgian,"The main event of UFC Vegas 109 is an exciting Middleweight clash, but one that the Bloody Elbow experts see as belonging to only one of the competitors. Two top ten Middleweight contenders face off in a bout that could have huge implications on the division, as Anthony Hernandez looks to add an eighth consecutive victory to his record. The fighter known as “Fluffy” will have to contend with Roman Dolidze, an impressive Georgian fighter who could be in a make-or-break situation in regards to his chances of being a top Middleweight fighter. The Bloody Elbow staff has made their predictions about what will happen in the main event of UFC Vegas 109 between Dolidze and Hernandez. - READ MORE – UFC Vegas 109 Full fight card as Roman Dolidze battles Anthony Hernandez in the Middleweight main event Roman Dolidze vs. Anthony Hernandez predictions Kye Dimond: “‘Fluffy’ Hernandez is just a nightmare in this division because of his gas tank. I can’t see Roman Dolidze putting him away early, so I’m expecting another middleweight Merab performance.” PREDICTION: ANTHONY HERNANDEZ VIA DECISION Ross Markey: “It seems like Anthony Hernandez is riding an almost unstoppable streak at the moment, regardless of who he is matched up with. And whether it’s against similar styles to his own or dynamic strikers, ‘Fluffy’ seems to prevail regardless. “Against Roman Dolidze, I’m picking Hernandez to endure an early onslaught from the Georgian en route to a late stoppage deep into their headliner.” PREDICTION: ANTHONY HERNANDEZ VIA STOPPAGE Hamish Woodward: Anthony Hernandez’s winning streak doesn’t look like it will come to an end at UFC Vegas 109, despite what should be a tough opponent in Roman Dolidze. His seven wins on the bounce must make him the favorite, especially against some impressive fighters like Roman Kopylov and Brendan Allen. He is a strong finisher who likes to put away fighters in the later rounds, and this bout should be no different. Expect a late finish win for Fluffy to move ever closer to a title fight in the future. PREDICTION: ANTHONY HERNANDEZ VIA STOPPAGE",2025-08-06,https://bloodyelbow.com/2025/08/06/roman-dolidze-vs-anthony-hernandez-bloody-elbow-predictions-suggest-that-fluffy-will-be-too-much-for-the-georgian/
Roman Dolidze vs. Anthony Hernandez announced as UFC Vegas 109 main event on Aug. 9,"Ultimate Fighting Championship (UFC) Middleweights will headline a Fight Night in “Sin City.” Roman Dolidze vs. Anthony Hernandez announced as UFC Vegas 109 main event on Aug. 9 No. 8-ranked Roman Dolidze will collide with No. 9-seeded Anthony Hernandez at UFC Vegas 109 on Sat., Aug. 9, 2025, inside the UFC Apex in Las Vegas, Nevada. Kevin K first reported the news. The two Middleweights were originally slated to clash at UFC 302 in June 2024, but Hernandez withdrew due to a torn hand ligament. Dolidze (15-3) enters the bout following a five-round unanimous decision victory over Marvin Vettori at UFC Vegas 104. The 36-year-old Georgian is riding a three-fight winning streak, with notable wins over Kevin Holland and Anthony Smith. UFC Vegas 109 marks Dolidze’s third UFC main event. Hernandez (14-2-1) is fresh off a unanimous decision win over Brendan Allen at UFC Seattle. “Fluffy” is enjoying the best run of his career, boasting a seven-fight winning streak with victories over Michel Pereira (watch highlights), Roman Kopylov, and Edmen Shahbazyan, among others. A victory over Dolidze could propel the 31-year-old into serious title contention, especially with the Middleweight division ripe for new challengers to face champion Dricus Du Plessis. Other fights announced for UFC Vegas 109 are the following: Eryk Anders vs. Christian Leroy Duncan Raffael Cerqueira vs. Julius Walker Julija Stoliarenko vs. Gabriella Fernandes Angela Hill vs. Iasmin Lucindo To checkout UFC’s upcoming schedule of events click here.",2025-05-25,https://www.mmamania.com/2025/5/25/24436795/roman-dolidze-vs-anthony-hernandez-announced-as-ufc-vegas-109-main-event-on-aug-9
Roman Dolidze vs Anthony Hernandez: Fight Overview,"9 Aug On August 9, the UFC Apex in Las Vegas will host a compelling middleweight matchup as Roman Dolidze faces Anthony Hernandez at UFC Fight Night. Both fighters are coming off decision victories and step into the Octagon with momentum and something to prove. Dolidze, known as ""The Caucasian,"" is coming off a hard-fought win over Marvin Vettori. The Georgian fighter, now 36, has built a reputation for combining physical strength with calculated pressure. With over half of his wins coming by knockout, Dolidze’s striking power is a key factor in any bout he enters. Across the cage stands Anthony ""Fluffy"" Hernandez, a versatile grappler with an unrelenting pace. His recent unanimous decision win against Brendan Allen showcased his ability to dictate rhythm and control exchanges on the ground. At 31, Hernandez is entering his prime, looking to climb higher in the rankings. The stylistic contrast is clear: Dolidze brings power and experience, while Hernandez leans on conditioning and submission threats. With both fighters sharing orthodox stances and similar physical dimensions, the difference may come down to timing and fight IQ. This bout is not for a title, but it carries serious implications for the middleweight pecking order. Expect a tactical, high-stakes contest between two contenders looking to break into the elite tier. The Tale of the Tape data is compiled from publicly available information on Sherdog | Roman Dolidze | Anthony Hernandez | |---|---| | Georgia | USA | | 15 - 3 - 0 (8 KOs) | 14 - 2 - 0 (3 KOs) | | middleweight (185 lbs / 83,9 kg) | middleweight (185 lbs / 83,9 kg) | | Age | | | Wins | | | Losses | | | Anthropometry | | The scheduled 5-round middleweight bout will take place on August 9, 2025. The full fight night schedule, including local start times for various countries, is listed below. Check the schedule to see when the event begins in your region. The fight night will start on Saturda